<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAFRICA'S M&amp;R FINALISES FEDSTONE DEAL.</title>
<headline>SAFRICA'S M&amp;R FINALISES FEDSTONE DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African holding firm Murray &amp; Roberts Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday it had finalised the sale of its Fedstone group of companies to Japan's Bridgestone Corp .</p>
<p>The deal, first announced last October, was for 290 million rand and the effective purchase date is now to be December 27, 1996. In addition to the cash Fedstone will repay M&amp;R's engineering unit an interest free loan of 70 million rand.</p>
<p>M&amp;R said the whole deal would cut its borrowings by 450 million rand and boost non-operating earnings buy 70 million rand.</p>
<p>Fedstone's largest unit is tyre group Firestone South Africa.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
